From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:57:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 735/743] perf: replay DSpark drafter metadata inside query
 graphs

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Experiment base: candidate-38 1f33102547e4da5c64712390604695d1abd577c4

Capture the existing DS41 integer metadata builder before the DFlash query
forward. Reuse the fixed graph shape and persistent device input/output
buffers so FULL replay can omit its eager Python metadata rebuild.
Context parallelism, model-state overrides and unsupported builders retain
that eager rebuild. No target verification, sampling, collective, scheduler
or copy-draft budget changes are intended.

Quality implications: the metadata kernel and its integer arithmetic are
unchanged. GPU graph equivalence, rank agreement, sampled output, cancellation,
streaming and two-boot performance remain qualification gates; no speedup is
claimed. Added CPU replay-order/guard regressions and a frozen-cache GPU
regression for changed lengths, padding and slot reuse.

Tests: 35 host graph tests passed in a CPU-only candidate-38 container;
focused new coverage: 9 passed, 3 CUDA tests skipped. Full pre-commit checks
pass after adapting two test calls to accelerator APIs. Preserve exact GPU
validation requirements in the companion deployment experiment.

Upstream status: experimental source-fork draft, not submitted to canonical
upstream; no deployment or promotion approval.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
